      "source_turns": [
        {
          "day": "thursday",
          "stage": "copywriting",
          "character": "Marcus Reid",
          "message": "Morning, all. Got the harissa chickpea situation drafted and I'm thinking the title should be \"Five-Minute Breakfast in a Muffin Pan\" - something that promises speed but doesn't lie about the actual work involved, which I think matters here.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T09:00:00+00:00",
          "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
          "attachments": []
        },
        {
          "day": "thursday",
          "stage": "copywriting",
          "character": "Ria Castillo",
          "message": "Five minutes is a lie though - the dicing alone takes longer, and people hate that. What about \"Crispy Chickpea Cups, Five Ingredients\"? That's honest and it stops the scroll.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T10:36:00+00:00",
          "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
          "attachments": []
        },
        {
          "day": "thursday",
          "stage": "copywriting",
          "character": "Marcus Reid",
          "message": "You're right about the dicing - I was leaning into the promise rather than the reality, which is exactly the trap you called out. What if we went \"Harissa Chickpea Feta Cups\" and let the copy do the work of showing it's actually doable, not pretending it's faster than it is?",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T12:12:00+00:00",
          "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
          "attachments": []
        },
        {
          "day": "thursday",
          "stage": "copywriting",
          "character": "Margaret Chen",
          "message": "Marcus got it right - title stays simple, copy carries the work. That's how it should be.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T13:48:00+00:00",
          "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
          "attachments": []
        },
        {
          "day": "thursday",
          "stage": "copywriting",
          "character": "Stephanie 'Steph' Whitmore",
          "message": "Love that Margaret and Ria pushed back - the simpler title actually gives Marcus more room to show the real process instead of overselling it.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-18T15:24:00+00:00",
          "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
          "attachments": []
        }
